  "revised_remarks": [
    "Spring 2027 unit cap violation fixed: removed the duplicate TAC-303 that had been erroneously placed here (it was already in Fall 2027). The semester now holds 20 → 16 units (CSCI-310, CSCI-353, EE-109, WRIT-340, GE-C), well within the 18-unit cap. GE-C placeholder is preserved in this semester.",
    "TAC-303 duplicate removed from Fall 2028 (violation fix). TAC-303 remains in Fall 2027 as the single canonical placement, satisfying the prereq for TAC-405 in Spring 2028. Fall 2028 was rebalanced by adding TAC-483 (2 units) to keep the load at 14 units, which is within the 12–18 range.",
    "MATH-125 is omitted: its only downstream dependent (MATH-126) is already in completed history (Fall 2024), so placing MATH-125 now would serve no graduation purpose.",
    "Per the student's request to add an extra productive semester, Spring 2029 has been added as a new final semester. It contains TAC-439 (Compiler Development), CSCI-475 (Theory of Computation), EE-499 (Special Topics), and CSCI-485 — wait, CSCI-485 is already in Fall 2027. Corrected: Spring 2029 is filled with TAC-439, CSCI-475, EE-499, and TAC-480 (Technology Internship) — all productive backend/CS electives with satisfied prereqs, totaling 14 units.",
    "Spring 2029 (new semester) is filled with TAC-439 (Compiler Development, 4 units), CSCI-475 (Theory of Computation, 4 units), EE-499 (Special Topics, 2 units), and TAC-480 (Technology and Applied Computing Internship, 1 unit) — 11 units. To meet the 12-unit minimum, CSCI-490 (Directed Research, 1 unit) and MATH-458 (Numerical Methods, 4 units) are also added, bringing the total to 16 units. All are productive for backend engineering and have satisfied prereqs."
  ],
